{"name":"Diablo Red","hex":"#cd0d01","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"diablo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The Devil or a devil."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Synonym of diable (“flavored with hot spices/sauces”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diablo"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Diablo (series)","blocks":[{"text":"Diablo is an action role-playing dungeon crawler video game series originally developed by Blizzard North and continued by Blizzard Entertainment after the original North studio shut down in 2005. The franchise is made up of the four main games: Diablo, Diablo II, Diablo III, and Diablo IV. Expansions include the third-party published Hellfire, which follows the first game; Lord of Destruction, published by Blizzard and released after the second game; Reaper of Souls, which follows the third game; Rise of the Necromancer which also follows the third game and Vessel of Hatred and Lord of Hatred, which follow the fourth game. Additional content is provided through story elements explored in other types of media forms."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Diablo_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diablo_(series)","wikidata":"Q44165"},{"title":"Diablo (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Diablo is a 1997 action role-playing game developed by Blizzard North and published by Blizzard Entertainment for Windows. It is the first installment in the video game series of the same name."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Diablo_Coverart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diablo_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q220960"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/Diablocharacter.png/330px-Diablocharacter.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/Diablocharacter.png/330px-Diablocharacter.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Promotional artwork released by Blizzard Entertainment, which depicts one incarnation of the franchise's eponymous villain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiablocharacter.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Diabloscreen.jpg/330px-Diabloscreen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Diabloscreen.jpg/330px-Diabloscreen.jpg